'''''Coronilla minima''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] from the family [[Fabaceae]] found in Eastern and Central [[Spain]].

== Description ==
The [[plant stem]]s are {{convert|5|-|60|cm}} long and are erect. Leaves grow in 2-4 pairs and are {{convert|0.8|-|2.2|mm}} long and membranous with {{convert|1.2|-|20|mm}} by {{convert|0.8|-|7|mm}} long obovate and spatulate leaflets.

The plant flowers in spring when the [[Inflorescence]] carries 4-12 flowers that have a {{convert|1.5|-|3.5|mm}} long [[Peduncle (botany)|peduncle]] which have ascending {{convert|0.4|mm}} bracteoles and are often deciduous. Pedicels are {{convert|1|-|3.5|mm}} long with {{convert|2|-|4|mm}} long [[Sepal|calyx]] that is glabrous. The Corolla is yellow in colour while the keels that are {{convert|4|-|6.5|mm}} by {{convert|1.5|-|2.1|mm}} have one [[awn (botany)|awn]] that is {{convert|2|-|2.5|mm}} long. The [[Fruit]]s are {{convert|10|-|45|mm}} in length and are straight, containing {{convert|1|-|1.1|mm}} by {{convert|3|-|3.8|mm}} transverse to ovoid seeds of a yellowish-brown colour.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.floravascular.com/index.php?spp=Coronilla%20minima|title=Coronilla minima L.|publisher=Flora Vascular|accessdate= February 15, 2014}}</ref>

